# Practice-review reminder: the QUARTERLY BACKSTOP for the practice-review
# skill (claude/skills/practice-review/SKILL.md in the kit, which lands as
# .claude/skills/practice-review/SKILL.md in a bootstrapped project).
#
# The practice review is the standing outward-facing meta-review of the
# operating model. It diffs the practices the shop actually runs (recorded
# in the skill's inventory.md) against external best practice and current
# AI-practitioner discourse, plus one inward loop-telemetry lens (mechanism
# decommission proposals, harness-primitive absorption, gate economics,
# metrics sunset). On the source project it was mechanized under the
# two-strikes rule: the only outward reviews ever taken were ad-hoc founder
# impulses on consecutive days, and both found real gaps that the
# inward-facing loops structurally cannot see (they audit conformance to
# the existing rules, not the rule-set's completeness).
#
# This cron is the quarterly backstop only. The other trigger, a new default
# model generation landing, cannot be scheduled; the skill carries it.
# Quarterly is deliberate: each run resets the baseline and the discourse
# does not move monthly. Running it more often manufactures noise, not
# signal. Tune the cadence if your project's evidence says otherwise.
#
# NON-GATING: scheduled and manual only. It files one issue with the default
# GITHUB_TOKEN and nothing else. It must never become a required check.
# Schedule caveats: GitHub runs schedules only from the default branch, the
# timing is best-effort, and GitHub suspends schedules after about 60 days
# without repo activity.
#
# BOARD DEPENDENCY: the issue reaches the project board only through the
# board's built-in "Auto-add to project" workflow (a web-UI setting with no
# API surface; kit README, "Post-bootstrap checklist"). Until that is on,
# the reminder lands off-board.
#
# OPT-IN: copy this file to the new project's
# .github/workflows/practice-review-reminder.yml. scripts/bootstrap.ps1 does
# not copy it, on purpose: a reminder is only useful once the skill's
# inventory.md exists and its tracker issue is open (the skill's adoption
# step). Fill the <PLACEHOLDER> below before the first tick.

name: Practice Review Reminder

on:
  schedule:
    # 06:18 UTC on the 1st of Jan/Apr/Jul/Oct: quarterly. Pick a minute
    # distinct from any other first-of-month reminder in the repo, so the
    # crons do not pile up on the same tick.
    - cron: '18 6 1 1,4,7,10 *'
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions:
  issues: write

jobs:
  remind:
    name: File the practice-review reminder issue
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 5
    steps:
      # No actions/checkout: the job is pure GitHub API traffic.
      - name: Create reminder issue unless one is already open or was recently closed
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          REPO="${{ github.repository }}"
          TITLE="Practice review due"

          # Idempotency guard 1: an open issue with this exact title means the
          # previous cycle is still pending. Skip instead of stacking.
          EXISTING=$(gh issue list --repo "$REPO" --state open \
            --search "in:title \"$TITLE\"" --json number,title --limit 20 \
            --jq ".[] | select(.title == \"$TITLE\") | .number" | head -1)
          if [ -n "${EXISTING:-}" ]; then
            echo "Open reminder issue #$EXISTING already exists. Skipping."
            exit 0
          fi

          # Idempotency guard 2 (anti-nag): skip if the last reminder closed
          # within 30 days. Guard 1 already covers the still-pending case, so
          # this guard only suppresses a re-nag right after an off-cadence
          # model-generation-triggered run. 30 days does that while making a
          # silently skipped quarter nearly impossible: a close would need to
          # land within 30 days of the NEXT tick to suppress it.
          RECENT_CLOSE=$(gh issue list --repo "$REPO" --state closed \
            --search "in:title \"$TITLE\"" --json number,title,closedAt --limit 20 \
            --jq ".[] | select(.title == \"$TITLE\") | .closedAt" | sort -r | head -1)
          if [ -n "${RECENT_CLOSE:-}" ]; then
            CLOSED_EPOCH=$(date -d "$RECENT_CLOSE" +%s)
            NOW_EPOCH=$(date -u +%s)
            AGE_DAYS=$(( (NOW_EPOCH - CLOSED_EPOCH) / 86400 ))
            if [ "$AGE_DAYS" -lt 30 ]; then
              echo "Last practice review closed $AGE_DAYS day(s) ago (< 30). Skipping, too soon to nag."
              exit 0
            fi
          fi

          BODY_FILE="$RUNNER_TEMP/practice_review_reminder_body.md"
          cat > "$BODY_FILE" <<'EOF'
          Time for the quarterly practice review: diff the operating model against external best practice and current AI-practitioner discourse, plus the inward loop-telemetry pass (mechanism decommission proposals, harness-primitive absorption, gate economics, metrics sunset).

          - **How to run it:** invoke the `practice-review` skill in Claude Code (`.claude/skills/practice-review/SKILL.md` owns the method: seal the detection key first, refresh `inventory.md`, run the pinned workflow, triage).
          - **Also runs off-cadence** when a new default model generation lands. If that happened recently and a review ran, close this issue.
          - The review is **catch-and-report**: recommendations reach the founder for triage; nothing is adopted or decommissioned without approval. Contradictions of decisions-of-record surface flagged with their strong reason, never silently.
          - Expect diminishing returns run over run. A thin run with real verification is a pass, not a failure to hunt harder.
          EOF

          # Milestone is best-effort: the no-milestone fallback keeps a renamed
          # or closed milestone from killing the reminder itself. Set it to
          # the project's inbox milestone (kit README, practice 1). If the
          # placeholder is left in place, the first create fails and the
          # fallback files the issue without a milestone.
          MILESTONE="<PLACEHOLDER: inbox milestone name, e.g. Code health / tech debt>"
          if gh issue create --repo "$REPO" --title "$TITLE" \
               --body-file "$BODY_FILE" --milestone "$MILESTONE"; then
            echo "Reminder issue created (milestone $MILESTONE)."
          else
            echo "Create with milestone failed (renamed/closed?). Retrying without."
            gh issue create --repo "$REPO" --title "$TITLE" --body-file "$BODY_FILE"
          fi
